WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.610
This video shows how to upload a large data file, such as
months of readings from a water-level logger.

00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:10.729
Open Upload data file from the Measurements
page.

00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:12.721
It has two parts.

00:00:12.841 --> 00:00:17.017
First you register the stations, then you add
their measurements.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.546
Choose Register stations, then your station
file.

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:27.906
Each row is one well: its name, type,
position, village and district.

00:00:28.026 --> 00:00:30.570
Here are three example wells.

00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:33.735
Press Register these stations.

00:00:33.855 --> 00:00:36.231
Then switch to Add measurements.

00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:40.647
Your new wells are on the map, each with its
own station code.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.767
The readings file must use these codes.

00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:46.671
Choose the readings file.

00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:52.023
This one is from one logger: forty-four
thousand, five hundred readings,

00:00:52.143 --> 00:00:55.431
one every five minutes for five and a half
months.

00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:59.367
The preview checks every row before anything
is saved.

00:01:00.183 --> 00:01:02.055
Press Import.

00:01:02.175 --> 00:01:06.855
A large file is sent once, and OurWater
imports it in steps.

00:01:06.975 --> 00:01:09.447
The bar shows how far it has got.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:12.519
Keep the page open until it finishes.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:18.678
When it finishes, you see how many
measurements went in: all forty-four thousand,

00:01:18.798 --> 00:01:21.126
five hundred and twenty-two of them.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.918
That is all it takes.

00:01:24.038 --> 00:01:30.038
If the connection drops part-way, choose the same
file again: readings already saved are skipped,

00:01:30.158 --> 00:01:32.558
so nothing is stored twice.

00:01:32.678 --> 00:01:35.342
Thanks for helping look after our water.
